<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for April 29.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for April 29.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the transport and pipeline arm of BG plc on Monday announced the following forecasts and data for gas consumption in the period 27-29 April.</p>
<p>DEMAND:</p>
<p>(mcm = million cubic metres)</p>
<p>Apr 27 (actual) 189 mcm, 44 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 28 (forecast) 200 mcm, 47 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>Apr 29 (forecast) 203 mcm, 47 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE:</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>Apr 27 (actual) 12.4 Celsius, SNT 10.9 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 28 (forecast) 12.2 Celsius, SNT 11.0 Celsius</p>
<p>Apr 29 (forecast) 11.3 Celsius, SNT 11.1 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption called for Monday, with none forecast for Tuesday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
